# Third-party game archives and extracted assets. Never tracked: redistribution
# is not ours to grant, and 195 MB of binaries poisons clone time for a repo
# whose tracked content is text.
/assets
fixtures/corpus/

# Design notes, decision records and the backlog. Present in the working tree
# and deliberately untracked: they are how the work is thought through, not what
# the work ships.
/docs

# Game executables, kept locally so key extraction has something to read.
# Never tracked: DR-006 keeps key material out of this repository, and an
# executable is where that material lives before it is extracted.
/bin

# Metadata payloads extracted from the corpus, addressed by `RPF_METADATA`.
# 10,144 files, 162 MB, and every one of them is shipped game data — the same
# content `assets/` is ignored for. Kept beside `assets/` and `bin/` because it
# is the third thing a gate names and the first two live here.
/metadata

# Extracted key material. Derived from a local game install; never redistributed.
# Anchored at the root: the rule is about a `keys/` directory beside `assets/`
# and `bin/`, and unanchored it also swallowed `crates/rpf-core/src/keys/`,
# which is source.
/keys/
*.keys

# Fuzzing corpora and findings. `cargo fuzz` writes both of these beside the
# targets, and **a seed corpus here is game data**: the metadata targets are
# seeded with 9,324 shipped `PSO` payloads and 388 `RBF` ones, which is the
# same content `assets/` is ignored for. A crash artefact is derived from one.
# Neither was ever tracked; this is what stops the first `git add -A` after a
# local run from doing it. DR-006.
fuzz/corpus/
fuzz/artifacts/
fuzz/coverage/

# Rust
target/
# `cargo-mutants` build output. Not tracked for `target/`'s reason, and
# named here because a sweep leaves it beside the source and `git add -A`
# would otherwise carry it onto a branch.
mutants.out/
**/*.rs.bk

# Node (editor client)
node_modules/
dist/
*.vsix

# A VS Code downloaded to run the editor tests in. Hundreds of megabytes, and
# re-downloaded on demand.
.vscode-test/

.DS_Store

# Scratch worktrees, made beside the checkout by tooling that works on a copy.
# Narrow rather than the whole directory, so a shared `.claude/settings.json`
# stays trackable if this project ever wants one.
.claude/worktrees/

# A mutation sweep in progress, and the partial results of the attempt before
# it. Kept out of the tree for `mutants.out/`'s reason — a sweep is measurement
# output, not source — and named by date so a finished one can be deleted.
/.sweep-*

# The working document that routes this repository's own work: authority order,
# repository policy, the rules the hooks enforce. Present in the working tree
# for the same reason `docs/` is, and untracked for the same reason — it is how
# the work is thought through, not what the work ships.
/AGENTS.md
